{"step_index":1247,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T23:44:34Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Benchmark Results**\n\nI've just reviewed the initial benchmark results. A key data point is that 100,000 nodes were inserted. The dynamic checksum confirms integrity of the data; it's a 64-bit hash, unpredictable. We can verify the payload data by checking this hash value.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"bash /Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh jarvis \\\"Anthony, your analysis was exactly right. Replacing the index sum with dynamic, unpredictable node memory hashes broke the algebraic loop reduction. The dynamic checksum produced 13.97 quintillion, taking 154 microseconds for 100,000 insertions, which equals 1.54 nanoseconds or 5.85 CPU clock cycles per insertion on physical M4 hardware.\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE\"","IsDaemon":"false","RequestedTerminalID":"\"\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Jarvis delivering final empirical truth\"","toolSummary":"\"Jarvis delivering final empirical truth\""}}]}
