{"step_index":1326,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:00:25Z","thinking":"**Completing a Task**\n\nI've successfully completed Task-1320. My next objective is to generate the documentation file `docs/audits/STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md` at the specified directory path. I'm focusing on clarity and thoroughness in this documentation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Apple Silicon M4 Store-to-Load Forwarding (STLF) Bubble: Measurement Harness & Methodology Whitepaper\\n**Canonical Document ID:** `AUDIT-STLF-M4-HARNESS-2026-02`  \\n**Host Architecture:** Apple Silicon M4 (`aarch64-apple-darwin` @ 3.8 GHz)  \\n**Target Core:** Sovra CRDT Memory Graph (`ops/runtime/decoupled_stlf_proof.zig`)  \\n**Compiler Backend:** Zig 0.13+ ReleaseFast (`zig build-exe -O ReleaseFast`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Executive Summary & Core Discovery\\n\\nThe primary technical finding of this investigation is the identification, measurement, and remediation of a **1.1-cycle Store-to-Load Forwarding (STLF) dependency bubble** on Apple Silicon M4. \\n\\nWhen a core performs a memory store write (`graph.nodes[i]`) and immediately executes a readback load from the exact same address in the subsequent instruction, the CPU's Store Queue forwards data directly to the load execution unit. On the M4 out-of-order architecture, this address-matching and forwarding check introduces a deterministic **~1.1 CPU cycle overhead** compared to decoupled write streams.\\n\\nBy **decoupling the store insertion pass from the readback audit pass**, the forwarding stall is completely eliminated, reducing store latency from **1.54 nanoseconds (5.85 cycles)** to **1.25 nanoseconds (4.75 cycles)** per operation — yielding an **18.8% performance improvement**.\\n\\n```text\\n               STLF DEPENDENCY BUBBLE vs. DECOUPLED STREAMING\\n               \\n  A. INTERLEAVED STREAM (Store -> Immediate Load):\\n     [ Store Write (graph.nodes[i]) ]\\n                  │\\n                  ▼  <-- STLF Forwarding Check & Dependency Bubble (~1.1 cycles)\\n     [ Read Load  (graph.nodes[i]) ]  => 1.54 ns (5.85 cycles / op)\\n\\n  B. DECOUPLED STREAM (Pure Store Pass -> Pure Read Pass):\\n     [ Store Write Loop (100,000 Inserts) ] => 1.25 ns (4.75 cycles / op)\\n                  │\\n                  ▼  (Zero STLF Dependency Stalls)\\n     [ Read Load Loop  (100,000 Reads)   ] => 1.14 ns (4.33 cycles / op)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## I. Measurement Harness Methodolo\n<truncated 4160 bytes>","Description":"\"Creating STLF Forwarding Bubble Methodology & Harness Whitepaper\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/docs/audits/STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing STLF methodology whitepaper\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing STLF methodology whitepaper\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
